From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 10:44:23 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] drm/virtio: export a dma-buf read-write

A GEM object keeps the first dma-buf exported from it, and the mode of
that export is the mode every later export gets. Guest Mesa's virgl
winsys exports without DRM_RDWR, so a buffer that Mesa exported first
can never be mapped writable through any dma-buf, even one a later
caller asked for with DRM_RDWR: Chromium's CPU upload into a
GpuMemoryBuffer and a VA driver writing an imported surface both fail
with EACCES.

Whoever can export the handle can already write the buffer through it,
so give every export O_RDWR. A caller that asked for a read-only file
gets a read-write one; nothing in the guest relies on the difference.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_prime.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_prime.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_prime.c
index 7334d253d36e91db16cbe97bab82d0fb7a974b0d..947892f8c8919600759811777ce95877dae64bc1 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_prime.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_prime.c
@@ -161,7 +161,15 @@ struct dma_buf *virtgpu_gem_prime_export(struct drm_gem_object *obj,
 
 	exp_info.ops = &virtgpu_dmabuf_ops.ops;
 	exp_info.size = obj->size;
-	exp_info.flags = flags;
+	/*
+	 * A GEM object keeps the first dma-buf exported from it, so the mode
+	 * of that first export is the mode every later one gets. Guest Mesa
+	 * exports without DRM_RDWR, which would leave every consumer that maps
+	 * the buffer for writing - an encoder input, a CPU upload - with a
+	 * read-only file. Anyone who can export the handle can already write
+	 * the buffer, so export it writable.
+	 */
+	exp_info.flags = (flags & ~O_ACCMODE) | O_RDWR;
 	exp_info.priv = obj;
 	exp_info.resv = obj->resv;
 
